  "term": "entorhinal cortex",
  "definition": "The entorhinal cortex is a region of cerebral cortex on the inner side of the parahippocampal gyrus, just behind the uncus’s olfactory cortex. It is the main starting point of nerve fibers that project to the hippocampal formation through the perforant pathway.",
